Package: scalableCounterfactual
Type: Package
Title: Scalable Counterfactual Distribution and Quantile Decomposition
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R: person("Yongrok", "Kim", email = "k3644366@sogang.ac.kr", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides modular estimators for counterfactual distributions and
    quantile decompositions following Chernozhukov, Fernandez-Val, and Melly
    (2013) <doi:10.3982/ECTA10582>. Conditional models and computation backends are configured
    independently. Supported models include quantile and censored quantile
    regression, location and location-scale models, distribution regression,
    and Cox duration regression. The quantile-regression backend provides
    weighted exact process solvers and the process-aware one-step approximation
    proposed by Chernozhukov, Fernandez-Val, and Melly (2022)
    <doi:10.1007/s00181-020-01898-0>.
    Inference includes checkpointed bootstrap, deterministic failed-draw
    replacement, pointwise and uniform bands, and functional KS/CMS tests.
    Large-sample features include bounded-memory marginalization, parallel
    execution, reproducible benchmarks, and optional CuPy CUDA computation.
    Quantile-crossing diagnostics, rearrangement, simulation validation,
    command-line adapters, and extension registries are included. The package
    core remains independent of application-specific variable names and sample
    definitions.
